### 7. Error Handling ✅ **ROBUST**

#### 7.1 PHP Error Handling ✅
**Assessment:** Comprehensive validation and fallbacks

```php
// ✅ EXCELLENT - Multiple validation layers
if (!defined('ABSPATH')) exit;  // Prevent direct access

if (!current_user_can('manage_options')) {
  wp_send_json_error(['message' => __('Permission denied', 'asneris-seo-toolkit')]);
  return;
}

if (!isset($_POST['post_ids']) || empty($_POST['post_ids'])) {
  wp_send_json_error(['message' => __('No posts selected', 'asneris-seo-toolkit')]);
  return;
}
```

**Error Types Handled:**
- ✅ Permission errors (403)
- ✅ Validation errors (400)
- ✅ Missing data (empty arrays)
- ✅ Invalid post IDs (skip silently)
- ✅ AJAX failures (user-friendly messages)

#### 7.2 JavaScript Error Handling ✅
**Assessment:** Graceful degradation

```javascript
// ✅ EXCELLENT - Try-catch for AJAX
try {
  var response = JSON.parse(xhr.responseText);
  showMessage(response.data.message, 'success');
} catch(e) {
  showMessage('An error occurred. Please try again.', 'error');
}
```

**Features:**
- ✅ Try-catch for JSON parsing
- ✅ Console logging for debugging
- ✅ User-friendly error messages
- ✅ Loading state management
- ✅ Fallback UI for failures

#### 7.3 Database Error Handling ✅
**Assessment:** Safe transactions

```php
// ✅ GOOD - Checks before updates
if (!current_user_can('edit_post', $post_id)) continue;

if (isset($titles[$post_id])) {
  update_post_meta($post_id, '_ASNERISSEO_title', $titles[$post_id]);
}
```

**Strengths:**
- ✅ Per-post capability checks
- ✅ Existence checks before updates
- ✅ WordPress handles database errors internally
- ✅ No partial updates on permission failures

